Z||000005||286SE'S||09-26-2001||03:40 PM||||If you have the delayed wipers it is possible that the wiper motor is causing the problem.<BR>The signal to the pump is routed through the circuit board on the motor. When you press the wash lever it runs the wipers 4 times then shuts them off. My washers did not work for a long time and when the delay died I replaced the circuit board but both problems still existed. Got a whole motor from the junkyard and installed it and both started working again normally. There is no wiper schematic in the Haynes book but the GM Fiero manual has it. Look in the archives as I remember someone posting it last year.<BR>Terry||||reg||14
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-26-2001||06:29 PM||||isthis...--I tried a brand new pump and it didn't work, either.<P>286SE'S--Exactly where is the circuit board on the pump motor?  This could easily be part of the problem as I have the "Fiero Phantom Wiper" syndrome, too.  This is bugging me.  I need to get it fixed before frost sets in.  (I generally clear the frost by using the w/w fluid.  Saves time in the mornings.)||||reg||1
